{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would conflict with the intent of Local Plan policy SC1and be unacceptable in principle, as it would involve the formation of self-contained residential units within the curtilage of existing dwellings and would fail to comply with other Development Plan policies.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed dwelling would be a visually intrusive, incongruous form of development which would represent a gross overdevelopment of an already heavily developed site and would conflict with the spacious suburban character of the local area. The proposal would conflict with Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development would cause significant harm to neighbouring living conditions at nos.156B and 160 Bedfont Lane by way of a loss of light and outlook and an increased sense of enclosure to both habitable rooms and rear gardens, contrary to Local Plan policy CC2.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development would offer a substandard quality of accommodation both internally and externally, as a result of concerns about light levels to habitable rooms, the usability of the proposed amenity space and the quality of access to the house, which would conflict with the intent of Local Plan policy SC5. "
  ],
